      "writtenOn": "2022-04-22T22:38:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Responding to comment from crrev/3587509: \"Oddly, the spec doesn\u0027t seem to contemplate this process failing, but I think we should be bailing out if we fail to transmit, similar to most of our other message sending states. (We don\u0027t seem to do this in Give_Battery_Status either. Maybe I\u0027m missing something.)\"\n\nDone. I have conditioned hard reset on a pd timer expiration or a protocol error like I see the other *_run functions in this file do.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4209,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4209,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "d1768b22816e3ed760ebcc3379137814137151ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28f63ad6_31dd5f18",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T21:59:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the timer getting started in this case?  \n\nWe\u0027ve hit discussions with this in the past regarding how the spec doesn\u0027t include any contingencies when transmitting doesn\u0027t succeed.  The majority of the time when we see this come up is when we\u0027re a sink and the source isn\u0027t permitting us to start an AMS.  In this case, since we\u0027re not starting an AMS we should be relatively safe assuming we can transmit.  \n\nThough if we receive a message and hit a discard, that would be an interruption to a non-interruptible AMS which has its own required treatment (see Table 6-72 Response to an incoming Message (except VDM))",
      "parentUuid": "82886938_68f77107",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4209,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4209,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "d1768b22816e3ed760ebcc3379137814137151ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5590893_d5c96e12",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-26T20:33:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for catching this. Looking more closely at the spec (8.3.2.10.2.1 Sink Gets Source Status and 8.3.2.10.2.2 Source Gets Sink Status), the Status sender\u0027s policy engine does not need to set a timer. I removed this condition for resetting. \n\nAlso, from Table 6-72 it looks like uninterruptible states related to setting power should hard reset and uninterruptible states which are not related to setting power should soft reset. Is that the correct reading? I updated `pe_give_status_run` to look for PE_FLAGS_PROTOCOL_ERROR and PE_FLAGS_MSG_DISCARDED. If either of those flags are set, it will soft reset because this is an uninterruptible AMS not related to setting power.",
      "parentUuid": "28f63ad6_31dd5f18",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4209,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 4209,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "d1768b22816e3ed760ebcc3379137814137151ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
